=== Style 1: advance until EOF ===
Token(type='KEYWORD', lexeme='let', line=1, col=1)
Token(type='IDENT', lexeme='x', line=1, col=5)
Token(type='EQ', lexeme='=', line=1, col=7)
Token(type='INT', lexeme='42', line=1, col=9)
Token(type='PLUS', lexeme='+', line=1, col=12)
Token(type='IDENT', lexeme='y', line=1, col=14)
Token(type='SEMICOLON', lexeme=';', line=1, col=15)

=== Style 2: peek then advance (decision before consuming) ===
peeked KEYWORD   -> consumed 'let'
peeked IDENT     -> consumed 'x'
peeked EQ        -> consumed '='
peeked INT       -> consumed '42'
peeked PLUS      -> consumed '+'
peeked IDENT     -> consumed 'y'
peeked SEMICOLON -> consumed ';'

=== Style 3: expect a specific sequence ===
let-binding: let x = 42
